You are a senior mobile UX designer.

Design a mobile app UI for a product called **“NoExcuse”**.


---

# 🎯 PRODUCT CONCEPT

NoExcuse is a task-based alarm app:

* Users set tasks with alarms
* They must COMPLETE the task (not dismiss alarm)
* Tasks may require verification (photo, steps)
* Users maintain streaks
* Optional penalty system (lose money if failed)

---

# 📱 SCREENS + STRUCTURE

---

## 1. SPLASH SCREEN

* App logo (center)
* App name
* Tagline (below)
* No actions

---

## 2. ONBOARDING FLOW (3 screens)

### Screen 1

* Title
* Short description
* Illustration placeholder
* Next button

### Screen 2

* Title
* Description (task completion concept)
* Illustration placeholder
* Next button

### Screen 3

* Title
* Description (penalty concept)
* CTA: Get Started

---

## 3. AUTH FLOW

### Login Screen

* Email input
* Password input
* Login button
* Link: Sign up

---

### Signup Screen

* Name input
* Email input
* Password input
* Goal selection (multi-choice list)
* Signup button

---

## 4. HOME DASHBOARD

Top section:

* Greeting (optional)
* Current streak display
* Motivation text

Main section:

* List of today's tasks (scrollable)

Each task item:

* Task title
* Time
* Status indicator (pending / done / missed)
* Quick action (complete or open)

Floating button:

* Add new task

---

## 5. CREATE TASK SCREEN

Inputs:

* Task title (text field)
* Time picker
* Repeat selector (daily/weekly/custom)

Verification type selector:

* None
* Photo proof
* Steps

Optional:

* Toggle: Enable penalty
* Input: penalty amount (if enabled)

CTA button:

* Create Task

---

## 6. ALARM ACTIVE SCREEN (CRITICAL UX)

Full-screen modal behavior

Display:

* Task title (large)
* Time or countdown
* Instruction text

Actions:

* Complete Task (primary)
* No simple dismiss option

If verification required:

* Redirect to verification flow

---

## 7. VERIFICATION FLOW

### Photo Verification

* Camera preview
* Capture button
* Retake option
* Submit button

---

### Steps Verification

* Progress indicator
* Required steps vs current
* Auto-complete when reached

---

## 8. SUCCESS SCREEN

* Success indicator (icon placeholder)
* Message: task completed
* Updated streak info
* CTA: Continue

---

## 9. FAILURE SCREEN

* Failure indicator (icon placeholder)
* Message: task missed
* If penalty enabled:

  * Show penalty info

CTA:

* Acknowledge / continue

---

## 10. STATS / STREAK SCREEN

* Current streak
* Longest streak
* Activity graph (weekly/monthly)
* Completion rate

---

## 11. PROFILE SCREEN

* User info
* Selected goal
* Settings list:

  * Notifications
  * Payments
  * Preferences
  * Logout

---

## 12. SUBSCRIPTION SCREEN

* Plan list
* Features comparison
* CTA: Upgrade

---

# 🔄 NAVIGATION STRUCTURE

Bottom navigation:

* Home
* Stats
* Profile

Global flows:

* Task creation (modal or separate screen)
* Alarm (full-screen override)

---

# 🎯 UX RULES

* User should NOT easily skip alarms
* Prioritize completion actions
* Keep flows short and direct
* Minimize friction in task creation
* Maximize friction in skipping tasks

---

# 📦 OUTPUT

Provide:

1. Screen-by-screen layout structure
2. Component hierarchy for each screen
3. Navigation flow diagram (text-based)
4. Interaction behavior (tap, swipe, transitions)


Focus purely on UX and structure.
